  "details": "- CVE-2026-53784: resolve the daemon module-root chdir through a trusted-owner\n  walk so a planted symlink on the module path or any parent component cannot\n  steer the daemon outside the module under \"use chroot = no\"\n- CVE-2026-53795: confine each side of do_rename_at()/do_link_at()\n  independently; an absolute --temp-dir or --link-dest previously disabled\n  confinement for the relative in-tree side as well\n- CVE-2026-53802: resolve operator-supplied input files (--filter merge files,\n  --files-from, --password-file, daemon secrets) through the trusted-owner walk\n  so a planted symlink cannot be read as filter rules or as the auth response\n- CVE-2026-53803: resolve operator-supplied output paths (--log-file,\n  --write-batch/--read-batch, daemon motd/lock/early-input/--config) through\n  the same walk, plus a regular-file-or-FIFO check on the --read-batch file",
